#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""The operator view. `design/loops.md` section 16.

Everything above it produces files; this is for the one human who has to
understand them. It is not a status page — several places in the design
*stop* until a person decides something, and if those are slow to reach you
the loops idle on provisional choices and the whole schedule is bounded by
how often you go reading JSON.

So the requirement is: everything a decision needs, on the page, next to the
decision. Answering happens here, and answering *is* the append to
`state/interventions.jsonl` — the log is the mechanism, not a record of it.

A trivial local server rather than a `file://` page, because a page opened
from disk cannot poll. The page asks for a version token every couple of
seconds and swaps the panels in place when it moves; a full reload would
reset the scroll position on a page you are reading while it updates.

Output is not written to disk. It is derived from state that is in git, and
regenerating per request is cheaper than owning a cache.

    harness/dashboard/serve [--port 8787] [--no-open]
"""

from __future__ import annotations

